          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) There are multiple ways to construct AʹBʹCʹDʹ in (i). Justify why the quadrilateral AʹBʹCʹDʹ you constructed is congruent to ABCD. You may need to show why S is collinear with the points Aʹ and Dʹ that you constructed, and similarly for P, Q and R. ("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Use congruence of triangles, for example ∆SDR ≅ ∆SDʹR. )"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.225,
            0.881,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Show that if PQRS is a square, then AC and BD are perpendicular and equal. Prove the converse."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.28,
            0.664,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12.4 Tiling the Plane Using Any 4-gon"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.314,
            0.883,
            0.412
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "There are many ways to tile the plane, using a single shape or multiple shapes, leading to beautiful pictures. These occur in mosaics in several ancient civilizations to more recent artwork, such as that of M.C. Escher, in nature (for example, a honeycomb) and in decorative patterns we encounter in daily life."
            }
          ]
        },
