          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We will see how the plane can be tiled with any given 4-gon, not just a parallelogram as we saw at the beginning of the chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.47,
            0.765,
            0.883,
            0.901
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Before you see the answer in Fig. 12.28, see the hints below and try to find a tiling using the given irregular 4-gon SOME. First, trace SOME on paper with its four angles labelled 1, 2, 3, 4. Remember that they add up to 360°. Cut out 15 identical copies."
            }
          ]
